        "r": 425.90110000000027,
        "b": 705.5587870854176
      },
      "content": "7. Generator Set/Regulator Tests",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0411",
      "reading_order": 433,
      "section": "GENERAL",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 140.0882,
        "t": 675.5514068359374,
        "r": 198.75619999999995,
        "b": 664.7321469606776
      },
      "content": "GENERAL",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0412",
      "reading_order": 434,
      "section": "GENERAL",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.56539999999998,
        "t": 652.6664068359376,
        "r": 291.53330000000034,
        "b": 579.5393492035389
      },
      "content": "The following tests and adjustments can be performed without disassembly of the generator set. These procedures should be used for testing the generator set components and the regulator in conjunction with the Troubleshooting Flow Charts in the generator set/Regulator Troubleshooting section."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0413",
      "reading_order": 435,
      "section": "GENERAL",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.565599999999996,
        "t": 565.0192068359376,
        "r": 291.47299999999973,
        "b": 479.2477519502828
      },
      "content": "WARNING Many  troubleshooting procedures present hazards that can result in severe personal  injury  or  death.    Only  qualified  service personnel with knowledge of fuels, electricity, and machinery hazards should perform service procedures.  Review safety precautions on inside cover page."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0414",
      "reading_order": 436,
      "section": "[A] TESTING FIELD VOLTAGE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 84.4725,
        "t": 463.5199068359375,
        "r": 254.3817,
        "b": 452.7006469606776
      },
      "content": "[A] TESTING FIELD VOLTAGE",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0415",
      "reading_order": 437,
      "section": "[A] TESTING FIELD VOLTAGE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.56539999999999,
        "t": 442.22240683593753,
        "r": 291.5696000000001,
        "b": 394.3227492035388
      },
      "content": "Field voltage can be tested at the brush holder terminals with a DC voltmeter.  Field voltage should fall between 18 and 60 volts.  Test at no load and at full load.  See Figure 7-1."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0022",
      "reading_order": 438,
      "section": "[A] TESTING FIELD VOLTAGE",
      "bbox": {
