        "b": 59.335556939887624
      },
      "content": "FIGURE 7-1. FIELD VOLTAGE TEST POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0417",
      "reading_order": 440,
      "section": "[B] TESTING GENERATOR SET ROTOR",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 330.6331,
        "t": 675.5514068359374,
        "r": 555.0091000000001,
        "b": 664.7321469606776
      },
      "content": "[B] TESTING GENERATOR SET ROTOR",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0418",
      "reading_order": 441,
      "section": "[B] TESTING GENERATOR SET ROTOR",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 654.5940068359375,
        "r": 565.1551000000003,
        "b": 568.7674492035388
      },
      "content": "The generator  set  circuits  can  be  tested  without having to disassemble the generator set.  It is recommended that an ohmmeter be used to check for open circuits and an insulation resistance meter for grounded circuits.  An ohmmeter can be used to check for grounded circuits, but it may not be able to detect marginal insulation breakdown."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0023",
      "reading_order": 442,
      "section": "[B] TESTING GENERATOR SET ROTOR",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 319.4518633551129,
        "t": 559.440653810073,
        "r": 563.9203154897939,
        "b": 317.8294892529957
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0023.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_0418",
      "next_block_id": "txt_0419"
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "id": "txt_0419",
      "reading_order": 443,
      "section": "[B] TESTING GENERATOR SET ROTOR",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 330.5197,
        "t": 304.0808068359375,
        "r": 553.3467000000003,
        "b": 295.0647569398876
      },
      "content": "FIGURE 7-2.  TESTING ROTOR FOR GROUNDS"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0420",
      "reading_order": 444,
      "section": "Testing for Grounds",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 271.0475068359375,
        "r": 435.81220000000013,
        "b": 260.22824696067755
      },
      "content": "Testing for Grounds",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0421",
      "reading_order": 445,
      "section": "Testing for Grounds",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 250.0901068359375,
        "r": 564.9603999999996,
        "b": 202.24764920353869
      },
      "content": "Check for grounds between each slip ring and the rotor shaft, Figure 7-2. Use a Megger or insulation resistance meter which applies 500 VDC or more at the test leads.  Perform test as follows:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0422",
      "reading_order": 446,
      "section": "Testing for Grounds",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2161,
        "t": 191.0729068359375,
        "r": 564.8053,
        "b": 168.51504920353864
      },
      "content": "Isolate the rotor windings by disconnecting the two leads to the brush holder."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0423",
      "reading_order": 447,
      "section": "Testing for Grounds",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 326.15369999999996,
        "t": 157.34030683593744,
        "r": 564.8096999999993,
        "b": 122.14014920353873
      },
      "content": "Connect test leads between each ring and the rotor  shaft  in  turn.    Meter  should  register 100,000 ohms or greater."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0424",
      "reading_order": 448,
      "section": "Testing for Grounds",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.215,
        "t": 110.96540683593742,
        "r": 564.7271999999996,
        "b": 88.40754920353868
      },
      "content": "If less than 100,000 ohms, rotor is questionable.  Thoroughly dry the rotor and retest."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0425",
      "reading_order": 449,
      "section": "Testing for Grounds",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.215,
        "t": 77.23280683593748,
        "r": 564.7601999999999,
        "b": 54.674949203538745
      },
      "content": "Replace a grounded rotor with a new identical part."
    }
  ]
}